        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you get oil completely out of concrete?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Usually, if the stain is recent. Oil that has sat for a few months often clears completely after repeated poultices or an enzyme treatment. Stains soaked into a slab for many years can leave a faint shadow even after careful work, since part of the oil sits deeper than any method reaches. For those, aim for a spot that blends in and no longer feels slick."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best powder for a concrete oil poultice?",
